<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Quintipartite Deed</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1676</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Quintipartite Deed of 1 July 1676 divided the English colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-jersey">New Jersey</a> into East Jersey and West Jersey. It was signed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-carteret">Sir George Carteret</a> and by the trustees of the Quaker proprietor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-byllynge">Edward Byllynge</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-penn">William Penn</a>, and set a dividing line from Little Egg Harbor to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delaware-river">Delaware River</a>. The two provinces were reunited as a single royal colony in 1702.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/quintipartite-deed.jpg" alt="Quintipartite Deed" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Scan by NYPL · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Province_of_New_Jersey,_divided_into_East_and_West,_commonly_called_the_Jerseys_(NYPL_b13504563-484192).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
